WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
How does adding more Lanes cause more traffic?&nbsp;
Take a city and a suburb. Between them is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.860
two-lane road a bike path and a train&nbsp;
line. Most people commute by bike or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.640
train. The two-lane road is jammed every&nbsp;
day, so the city widens it to four lanes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.480
The road is no longer jammed. Now Karen and&nbsp;
her 50 friends can all take their kids to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.320
school by car. Now a hundred rail commuters&nbsp;
can drive so they aren't dependent on train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.760
schedules. Now 20 cyclists can drive because&nbsp;
it's faster. The four-lane road becomes jammed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.680
so the city widens it to six lanes. The road is&nbsp;
no longer jammed. Now 20 commuters can drive on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.580
company fuel allowance instead of riding a&nbsp;
bike. Now a hundred rail commuters can drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.960
so they aren't dependent on train schedules. Now&nbsp;
50 high school students can drive instead of bike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.860
or train because it's faster. Due to lower&nbsp;
ridership and revenue, the train line cuts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.300
connections. Schedules become infrequent and&nbsp;
impractical, so 200 rail commuters switch from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.920
train to car. The six lane road is jammed every&nbsp;
day, so the city widens it to eight lanes, and so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.880
on until you have the Katy Freeway. And this is&nbsp;
how adding more Lanes only causes more traffic.

